  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "What is a community?",
      "a": "A community is a group of people who live in the same place or share something, and who help and depend on each other. Your street, village, school or town can all be communities.",
      "asks": [
        "Tell me about your home",
        "What does community mean?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "How does food reach my home?",
      "a": "A farmer grows it, drivers carry it, a shop or market sells it, and your family buys it. Many people in a chain work together so food reaches your plate.",
      "asks": [
        "Tell me about the farmer",
        "Where does my food come from?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Why do teachers matter to a community?",
      "a": "Teachers help children learn to read, count and think, so they can grow up and do all the other jobs a community needs, from doctor to builder.",
      "asks": [
        "Tell me about the teacher",
        "Why do we need teachers?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "What does a doctor do for a community?",
      "a": "A doctor helps sick people get better and helps healthy people stay well, for example with check-ups and vaccines. A healthy community can work, learn and play.",
      "asks": [
        "Tell me about the doctor",
        "Why do we need doctors?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "q": "Why do people in a community depend on each other?",
      "a": "Nobody can do every job well. When each person does one job and shares the results, everyone gets food, learning, health and transport. This is called interdependence.",
      "asks": [
        "What is interdependence?",
        "Why can we not do everything ourselves?"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    "Splitting work into different jobs is called division of labour; Adam Smith wrote about it in 1776.",
    "More than half of the world's people, about 57 percent in 2023, live in towns and cities (World Bank)."
  ],
